      <h3>Measure the errors</h3>
      <div class="label-input">
        <span>Published test labels enter here</span><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
      </div>
      <p class="score-rule">
        Predicted Exact<br /><span aria-hidden="true">≠</span><br />Published S, C or I
      </p>
      <p>
        Count label disagreements in the priority queue; calculate the random policy’s expected
        count.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="project-caption">
    Training labels fit the classifier; validation selects the model. This diagram shows the later,
    frozen test evaluation. Published test labels score the review policy only after its selection
    rule is fixed. A disagreement is a model error under the benchmark, not proof that the original
    label is wrong.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

